  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Dehydration of alcohols&nbsp;involves the formation of carbocation intermediate and this carbocation&nbsp;rearrange to form more stable carbocation which looses proton to form a more stable alkene.</p><p>In the following dehydration&nbsp;reaction also initially a secondary carbocation is formed which undergoes methyl shift to form a more stable tertiary carbocation which looses proton to form a stable&nbsp;alkene.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0077_a529242c04c8.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 229px;\" /></p>"
